# Blog visual system (Profit Media)

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-blog-cover-visual-system-design.md`

When creating or replacing blog covers / mid-article figures, follow this system. Do not invent a new style.

## Formats

| Role | Size | Aspect |
|------|------|--------|
| Card / OG square | `1024×1024` | 1:1 |
| Hero / OG wide | `1536×1024` | 3:2 |
| Inline in article | `1200×675` | ~16:9 |

Full-bleed. No white inset box on a lavender card frame.

## Brand tones

- Purple `#651561` family, yellow `#fcc000`, soft lilac wash
- No generic teal/cyan SaaS rainbow looks

## Modes (rotate)

- **A (~70%)** simplified illustration: 1 idea, 3–5 large shapes, thumbnail-readable
- **B (~30%)** editorial photo + purple/yellow duotone + at most one large graphic accent

## Language on art (site is HE + RU)

- Prefer **no words** on the image
- Allowed Latin only for industry acronyms readers already use: `CPL`, `CAC`, `Meta`, `A/B`, `₪`
- Do **not** put English UI words like `HOME`, `LANDING`, `MEDIA`, `MANAGEMENT`, full sentences
- Do not put Hebrew-only or Russian-only labels on shared covers (one art file serves both locales)

## Inline figures

- Use `<figure class="blog-inline-figure">` + bilingual captions in each locale file
- Place after a concept section (cost split, channel choice, funnel), not randomly
- Same visual rules as covers: large shapes, brand tones, little/no text

## Card test

If the idea is unclear at ~300px phone width, simplify.
